# Code owners for release and supply-chain surfaces.
#
# Changes to these paths alter what gets built, published, or trusted: CI
# workflows and guardrail scripts, dependency manifests and the lockfile,
# license/advisory policy, release playbooks, git hooks, and the security
# policy. They need a designated reviewer rather than any available approver.
# Maintainers can extend the owner list; ownership here does not replace the
# branch-protection rules configured in the repository settings.

/.github/                     @adrienlacombe
/.githooks/                   @adrienlacombe
/tools/                       @adrienlacombe
/Cargo.toml                   @adrienlacombe
/Cargo.lock                   @adrienlacombe
/crates/*/Cargo.toml          @adrienlacombe
/crates/controller/Cargo.toml @adrienlacombe
/deny.toml                    @adrienlacombe
/docs/crates-release.md       @adrienlacombe
/docs/supply-chain.md         @adrienlacombe
/SECURITY.md                  @adrienlacombe
